    <string name="plans_empty_hint">Just tell Bothy. When a plan comes due, Bothy pops up a card and reads it out to you:</string>
    <string name="plans_example_parcel">“Remind me to pick up the parcel in two hours”</string>
    <string name="plans_example_badge">“Remind me to bring my badge at 8 every weekday morning”</string>
    <string name="plans_example_fare">“Tell me when flights from Shenzhen to Chengdu drop below 800 yuan”</string>
    <string name="plans_example_weather">“Read me the weather at 8 every morning”</string>
    <string name="plans_example_umbrella">“Remind me to take an umbrella when it rains”</string>
    <string name="plans_example_air">“Remind me to open the windows when the air gets better”</string>
    <string name="plans_footer">When a plan comes due, Bothy pops up a card and reads the reminder out; a “Task” plan has Bothy run a turn; an “Auto” plan runs its actions directly, without the model. What status plans can watch depends on the MCP services loaded now (Settings → Connections → MCP or Connect apps): resources are read at the set interval, and services that only offer query tools are called at the interval (at most once every 5 minutes); this happens only while Bothy is running. A one-off reminder missed while the device was off is caught up if it starts within 2 hours; after that it is marked missed.</string>

